<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia peso closes lower.</title>
<headline>Colombia peso closes lower.</headline>
<dateline>BOGOTA 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Colombia's peso fell 1.05 to 1,003.54 pesos to the dollar as markets reopened after a two-day Christmas break.</p>
<p>The market was swamped with greenbacks but the central bank managed to push down the peso, in line with its crawling peg devaluation, by stepping in and buying dollars -- at least $72 million according to interbank traders.</p>
<p>The central bank, as is customary, declined to comment on the extent of its intervention.</p>
<p>The peso sank to an intraday low of 1,003.55 and hit an intraday high of 1,003.52. Dealers reported 92 trades worth a total $184 million.</p>
<p>--Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944</p>
